                    text: "**Global customers adding a second source outside China**: India overtook China as the largest exporter of smartphones to the US in the September 2025 quarter (IBEF), and the exporters here grew fast in Q1 (Syrma's exports +61%, Avalon's US customers 59% of sales, Cyient DLM 94% exported). **Defence and space**: figures from Deloitte and FICCI-EY used by Centum put India's defence production at about ₹1.54 lakh crore in FY25 and about ₹3 lakh crore by FY29, some 18% a year; Centum's order book is ₹1,797cr and Vinyas's ₹1,309cr (March 2026). **Air conditioners**: ICRA says room-AC volumes peaked at 12.5–13 million units in FY25, fell in FY26 on a weak summer and should grow 10–12% a year from here. **Lithium batteries** are replacing lead-acid: Maxvolt cites industry reports putting India's lithium-ion battery market at about US$2.3bn in 2022 and US$5.8bn by 2028 (17% a year), and says a rule moving e-rickshaws to lithium now starts in April 2028, a year later than planned. **AI data centres** pull demand for power electronics and memory (Aimtron's US UPS contract, Avalon's HVDC work, Sahasra's memory exports), but they also cause the shortages below. **My view: exports and defence are the durable drivers; air conditioners are the cyclical one.**",
