                    text: "**Amber** holds 26–27% of India's room-AC market (CRISIL), makes about 70% of an air conditioner's parts in-house and supplies brands covering about 75% of the market. **PG Electroplast** is taking share: its AC revenue grew 38% in Q1 against industry volume growth of about 15%, as brands find outsourcing cheaper than running their own plants. **Syrma** says it is the first or second vendor at most of its Indian customers but has only 1–2% of the spend at its global ones. Scale buys parts cheaper and gives brands a reason to stay, but it does not set the price: brands split orders, and new capacity keeps arriving (L&T has commissioned an EMS plant; Dixon and Tata Electronics are expanding). **My view: scale protects share, not margin.**",
